    <li><a href={books.pml1.url}>{books.pml1.full.en}</a> <span class="where">§5.5.3–5.5.4 (NHST and p-values) and §4.7.4–4.7.5 (confidence intervals).</span></li>
    <li><a href={books.pml2.url}>{books.pml2.full.en}</a> <span class="where">§3.10 (hypothesis testing).</span></li>
    <li><a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/00031305.2016.1154108">Wasserstein, R. L. and Lazar, N. A. (2016). The ASA Statement on p-Values: Context, Process, and Purpose. The American Statistician, 70(2), 129–133.</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s10654-016-0149-3">Greenland, S. et al. (2016). Statistical tests, P values, confidence intervals, and power: a guide to misinterpretations. European Journal of Epidemiology, 31(4), 337–350.</a></li>
  </ul>
</ConceptLayout>
